348
00:31:17,381 --> 00:31:26,380
Rust is the result of a chemical reaction in which the 26 electrons within the iron atom again come into play.

349
00:31:26,381 --> 00:31:31,460
Two of those electrons orbit the nucleus farther away than the rest.

350
00:31:32,420 --> 00:31:34,080
These electrons are sort of like black sheep.

351
00:31:34,880 --> 00:31:39,160
It would make the iron molecule a lot more stable if these electrons would go away, basically.

352
00:31:39,880 --> 00:31:44,740
Oxygen, on the other hand, needs a couple of electrons, so it's very eager to take them.

353
00:31:44,800 --> 00:31:50,860
So what happens is they come together, they combine, and they form a new compound called iron oxide.

354
00:31:52,180 --> 00:31:54,860
And that's iron's arch enemy, rust.

